{"seconds": 39.6, "exit": 0, "final": "So Nd5 would check the king on f6. After the forced king move, Nc7+ forks the king again AND attacks the undefended b5 pawn. This is a classic knight fork! The winning line is:\n\n**1. Nd5+ Ke6 (or Ke5/Kg7 all lose the b5 pawn) 2. Nc7+ and White wins the b5 pawn with a fork.**\n\nNow let me write the coaching note and provide the answer:\n\n**Best Move:** Nd5+\n\n**Main Line:** Nd5+ Ke6 Nc7+ Kd7 (or Ke5/Ke7) Nxb5\n\n**Motif:** fork (knight forks king and pawn; also forces the king to bad squares)\n\n**Coaching Note for Club Player:**\nWhen your opponent's knight just moved, check if your knight can give check and create a follow-up fork. Here, Nd5+ forces the Black king to move, then Nc7+ attacks both the king AND the undefended b5 pawn\u2014a classic knight fork. Always look for this pattern: a forcing check followed by attacking two pieces at once. Black cannot defend the pawn, so you win material cleanly. Watch for checks that lead to forks!\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Nd5+\", \"line\": [\"Nd5+\", \"Ke6\", \"Nc7+\", \"Kd7\", \"Nxb5\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "8/5p2/5k2/1p4nP/1N4PK/8/8/8 w - - 1 60"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "8/5p2/5k2/1p4nP/1N4PK/8/8/8 w - - 1 60"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "8/5p2/5k2/1p4nP/1N4PK/8/8/8 w - - 1 60", "square": "g5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "8/5p2/5k2/1p4nP/1N4PK/8/8/8 w - - 1 60", "square": "b4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "8/5p2/5k2/1p4nP/1N4PK/8/8/8 w - - 1 60", "square": "h4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "8/5p2/5k2/1p4nP/1N4PK/8/8/8 w - - 1 60"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/5p2/5k2/1p4nP/1N4PK/8/8/8 w - - 1 60", "move": "Nd5+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/5p2/5k2/1p4nP/1N4PK/8/8/8 w - - 1 60", "m